# SPDX-License-Identifier: 0BSD
#
# Omarchy Mobile build of libcamera for the Pixel 7 Pro (gs201 CSIS receiver).
#
# Derived from Arch Linux's libcamera PKGBUILD, tag 0.7.2-4
# (https://gitlab.archlinux.org/archlinux/packaging/packages/libcamera, 0BSD),
# which Arch Linux ARM builds unchanged for aarch64. Omarchy Mobile changes:
#  - 0001-pipeline-simple-Add-the-Google-gs201-CSIS-receiver.patch: one
#    entry in the simple pipeline handler's supportedDevices table, so a
#    media device whose driver is "gs201-csis" is matched, with the software
#    ISP on (device/cheetah/CAMERA-PLAN.md, 5.2). Send upstream together
#    with the kernel driver; drop it once libcamera ships the entry.
#  - aarch64 only. Pipelines simple and uvcvideo (USB cameras through
#    USB-C), IPA simple only: none of the other aarch64 pipelines (rkisp1,
#    rpi/*, imx8-isi, mali-c55) can match on this phone, and a smaller
#    native build.
#  - softisp-gpu forced on, so a missing EGL fails the build instead of
#    silently leaving the GPU debayer out. At runtime the GPU path is
#    tried first and falls back to the CPU; LIBCAMERA_SOFTISP_MODE=cpu
#    forces the CPU path.
#  - No documentation (no libcamera-docs split, no Doxygen, Sphinx or
#    TeX Live in the build) and no test suite (test=false, no check()).
#  - werror=false: GCC 16's -Warray-bounds flags libstdc++'s own std::mutex
#    construction in camera_manager.cpp and log.cpp (a false positive in the
#    library headers), which -Werror turned into a failed build.
#  - 0002-libcamera-Add-the-Sony-IMX386-sensor.patch: the IMX386's sensor
#    helper (black level, the gain model measured in CAM4.3c), properties
#    and an uncalibrated simple-IPA tuning file (CAMERA-PLAN.md CAM5).
#  - 0003-ipa-simple-agc-Step-faster-when-far-from-the-target-.patch: the simple
#    IPA's AGC steps with a proportional gain of 0.1 instead of 0.04 while
#    the exposure error is above 1, so a dark start settles in about a
#    second (CAMERA-PLAN.md CAM5.2d).
#  - 0004-libcamera-Add-the-Samsung-S5KGN1-sensor.patch: the main camera's
#    sensor helper (black level 64 at 10 bits, gain code / 32), properties
#    (1.2 um cell, two-frame delays) and a tuning stub.
#  - 0005-libcamera-software_isp-add-contrast-autofocus.patch (Robin
#    Snyders): contrast autofocus in the simple IPA. The simple pipeline
#    hands it the focus lens found through the sensor's ancillary link
#    (DT lens-focus) and applies its V4L2_CID_FOCUS_ABSOLUTE.
#  - 0006-software_isp-Focus-on-the-frame-centre-with-statisti.patch: the
#    sharpness is measured over the centre of the frame; statistics come
#    every frame on a camera with a lens (every fourth without); the lens
#    is driven only while Af runs and only on a change; step counts and
#    range from the tuning file.
#  - 0007-software_isp-Steadier-contrast-autofocus.patch (cube oakley):
#    lens settling before samples, a parabola fit of the peak, a smoothed
#    continuous mode that does not hunt, scans on settled exposure.
#  - 0008-software_isp-Keep-exposure-white-balance-and-focus-a.patch (cube
#    oakley): a reconfiguration of the same mode (a still after a
#    preview) keeps AGC, AWB and focus instead of starting over.
#  - 0009-software_isp-Take-contrast-and-saturation-defaults-f.patch (cube
#    oakley): Adjust reads contrast and saturation defaults from tuning.
#  - 0010-software_isp-Gather-GPU-statistics-over-the-visible-.patch (cube
#    oakley): with the GPU debayer and an output smaller than the sensor
#    mode, 3A saw only the top-left corner of the frame.
#  - 0011-ipa-simple-agc-Add-digital-gain-past-the-sensor-s-li.patch: up to
#    4x digital gain once exposure and analogue gain are at their limits.
#  - 0012-ipa-simple-Tune-the-Pixel-7-Pro-s-ultrawide-and-main.patch: Af on
#    both cameras, the IMX519 colour matrices from libcamera's Raspberry
#    Pi tuning (BSD-2-Clause) as a stand-in for the IMX386, contrast and
#    saturation defaults.
#  - 0013-libcamera-Add-the-Samsung-S5K3J1-and-S5KGM5-sensors.patch: the
#    front and telephoto cameras' sensor helpers (black level 64 at 10
#    bits, gain code / 32), properties and tuning files (identity colour
#    matrix, contrast and saturation defaults, Af on the telephoto).
#  - 0014-pipeline-simple-Accept-a-sensor-configuration-within.patch: a
#    sensor mode whose output is within 1% of the stream qualifies, so the
#    front camera's 1080p video runs its binned mode (1912x1080) instead of
#    the full-resolution one.
#  - 0015-ipa-simple-agc-Step-out-of-a-pinned-histogram-quickl.patch: while
#    nearly every pixel is in the darkest or brightest histogram bin, the
#    AGC doubles or halves the exposure each step (the front camera took
#    seconds to brighten from its starting exposure).
#  - 0016-software_isp-debayer_egl-Destroy-the-EGL-context-whe.patch: the
#    GPU debayer's EGL context is destroyed at stop; abandoned contexts kept
#    the last buffers imported, and a camera app leaked 290 MiB of
#    contiguous memory until starts failed to allocate.
#  - 0017-ipa-simple-agc-Judge-only-frames-taken-with-the-last.patch: the
#    AGC judges only frames taken with its last request (and one more), so
#    a sensor slower than modelled no longer makes it oscillate between a
#    white and a black picture outdoors; pinned steps x8 and 1/16.
#  - 0018-ipa-simple-Carry-the-exposure-over-to-another-mode-o.patch: a
#    switch to another mode of the same sensor (a full-resolution still
#    from a binned preview) keeps the converged exposure in time and gain
#    and the white balance, instead of starting at the mode's longest.
#  - 0019-ipa-simple-agc-Report-the-AE-state.patch: AeState (searching,
#    converged), so an application can wait for the exposure to settle
#    before keeping a still.
#  - 0020-ipa-simple-agc-Add-exposure-compensation.patch: ExposureValue, -2
#    to +2 stops.
#  - 0021-ipa-simple-Take-the-sensor-mode-s-timings-at-configu.patch: the
#    IPA takes the configured sensor mode's line length and pixel rate, so
#    exposure times are right in every mode.
#  - 0022-ipa-simple-agc-Support-manual-exposure-time-and-anal.patch:
#    ExposureTimeMode, AnalogueGainMode, ExposureTime, AnalogueGain and
#    AeEnable: manual shutter and ISO, and an exposure lock.
#  - 0023-ipa-simple-awb-Support-manual-white-balance.patch: AwbEnable,
#    ColourGains and, where the tuning file has a ctCurve (the IMX386),
#    ColourTemperature.
#  - 0024-software_isp-Gather-focus-statistics-over-a-window-t.patch: the
#    focus statistics window moves, with a luminance histogram over it.
#  - 0025-ipa-simple-Focus-and-meter-on-the-application-s-wind.patch:
#    AfMetering and AfWindows (tap to focus), and AeMeteringMode (matrix,
#    spot, centre-weighted) on that window.
#  - 0026-ipa-simple-af-Support-pausing-continuous-autofocus.patch: AfPause
#    in continuous autofocus (a focus lock).
#  - 0027-ipa-simple-Support-FrameDurationLimits.patch: FrameDurationLimits
#    per configured mode, through VBLANK (60 fps video).
#  - 0028-software_isp-Correct-lens-shading-with-a-radial-mode.patch: a
#    radial lens shading correction in the GPU debayer, with coefficients
#    from the tuning file (LensShading).
#  - 0029-software_isp-debayer_egl-Add-a-noise-reduction-and-s.patch: a
#    second GPU pass for luma noise reduction and sharpening.
#  - 0030-ipa-simple-Add-noise-reduction-and-sharpening.patch: the Detail
#    algorithm drives that pass, scaled with the gain, and the Sharpness
#    control.
#  - 0031-software_isp-Gather-grey-candidates-for-white-balanc.patch: grey-
#    candidate sums in the statistics.
#  - 0032-ipa-simple-awb-Use-the-grey-candidates-and-smooth-th.patch: the
#    grey world over grey candidates, and smoothed gains: no colour cast
#    from grass or sky.
#  - 0033-ipa-simple-agc-Protect-the-highlights.patch: the AGC keeps clipped
#    highlights to about 2% of the picture (10% backlit).
#  - 0034-software_isp-debayer_egl-Clip-highlights-to-neutral.patch: clipped
#    highlights fade to neutral instead of cyan.
#  - 0035-ipa-simple-af-Scan-less.patch: faster autofocus: early stop,
#    narrower fine scan, local rescans in continuous mode.
#  - 0036-ipa-simple-agc-Aim-the-mean-luminance-at-20.patch: the AGC aims
#    the mean linear luminance at 20% of full scale instead of the middle of
#    a coarse histogram (stills were 1.5 stops bright).
#  - 0037-ipa-simple-agc-Count-highlights-as-they-come-out.patch: the
#    highlight cap counts what comes out clipped after the gains and the
#    tone curve, not the raw top; backlit only with 60% of the picture dark.
#  - 0038-ipa-simple-agc-Take-a-mode-change-gently.patch: after a mode
#    change, wait two frames more and move at most a stop on the first
#    judgement.
#  - 0039-ipa-simple-Hand-tune-the-Pixel-7-Pro-s-Samsung-senso.patch: a
#    hand-tuned colour matrix for the Samsung sensors (no chart):
#    saturation, greens, and the green cast off neutrals.
#  - 0040-ipa-simple-af-Settle-less-for-fine-steps.patch: fewer settle
#    frames for fine autofocus steps.
#  - 0041-ipa-simple-agc-Don-t-climb-back-into-the-clipping.patch: after a
#    highlight cut the exposure stays under 85% of the one that clipped,
#    loosening slowly: no bouncing on small bright lights.
#  - 0042-ipa-simple-Start-a-new-configuration-at-the-carried-.patch: a new
#    configuration starts the sensor at the carried exposure, set before
#    streaming (stills from the first frames came out at the mode's longest
#    exposure).
#  - 0043-software_isp-debayer_egl-Roll-highlights-off-and-kee.patch: a
#    highlight shoulder after the colour matrix and hue-preserving gamut
#    mapping instead of per-channel clipping; the neutral fade only where
#    the sensor clipped.
#  - 0044-ipa-simple-agc-Count-clipping-through-the-highlight-.patch: the
#    AGC counts clipping through the shoulder.
#  - 0045-ipa-simple-Soften-the-Samsung-sensors-hand-tuned-col.patch: the
#    hand-tuned Samsung matrix softened by 30%.
#  - 0046-software_isp-Count-the-samples-the-sensor-saturated.patch: the
#    statistics count the samples the sensor saturated.
#  - 0047-ipa-simple-agc-Mind-what-the-sensor-saturates-and-th.patch: the
#    highlight cap counts sensor saturation and sRGB 240, and grades its
#    limits by the mean of the rest (lamps, backlit subjects).
#  - 0048-software_isp-debayer_egl-Fade-sensor-clipped-highlig.patch: the
#    fade to neutral of sensor-clipped highlights starts at 80%, gently: no
#    hard ring in a clipped sky.
#  - 0049-software_isp-Gather-a-histogram-of-each-sample-s-bri.patch: the
#    statistics gather a histogram of each sample's brightest colour.
#  - 0050-ipa-simple-agc-Choose-the-exposure-on-the-predicted-.patch: the
#    AGC chooses the exposure on the predicted output (mean at sRGB 102,
#    highlights within 2% beyond unsalvageable light sources): no hunting.
#  - 0051-software_isp-debayer_egl-Add-hue-vibrance-and-a-tone.patch: hue,
#    vibrance and a shadow-lifting tone curve in the GPU debayer.
#  - 0052-ipa-simple-Add-the-Look-algorithm-and-tune-it-on-the.patch: the
#    Look algorithm, tuned for the four cameras on paired daylight shots.
#  - 0053-software_isp-debayer_egl-Smooth-the-chroma.patch: luma-guided
#    chroma noise reduction over a 9x9 footprint in the GPU's second pass.
#  - 0054-pipeline-simple-Pass-the-start-controls-to-the-softw.patch: the simple pipeline hands
#    the controls Camera::start() gets to the software ISP's IPA with the
#    first request (the preview kept a burst's manual exposure).
#  - 0055-software_isp-debayer_egl-Correct-defective-pixels-be.patch: defective
#    pixel correction before the debayer, on the packed bytes (a hot pixel
#    on the main camera showed as a magenta spot in every photo).
#  - 0056-libcamera-Add-the-Samsung-S5KGN8-sensor.patch: the Pixel 9a's main
#    camera: its black level (64 at 10 bits, measured), linear gain and an
#    uncalibrated tuning file (it ran with no helper before).
#  - pkgrel 4.22, so it sorts above Arch Linux ARM's 0.7.2-4.
#
# Maintainers of the original: David Runge, Carl Smedstad.

pkgbase=libcamera
